# ============================================================================
# SearchLab - environment variables
# ============================================================================
#
# You do NOT need to create a `.env` file to run this project.
#
# There is exactly ONE variable: VITE_ENGINE_URL
#
# It tells the frontend where to send code for execution. The correct value
# depends on where the app is running:
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNNING ON YOUR LAPTOP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Do nothing. Leave this file alone and do not create a `.env`.
#
#   With no `.env`, the code automatically uses the local engine:
#       http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
#   Start the engine first:
#       python python_engine.py
#
#   -> Python AND Java both work locally.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNNING ON VERCEL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Set this variable in the Vercel dashboard, NOT in a file:
#
#       Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#       Name:  VITE_ENGINE_URL
#       Value: /api
#
#   Then REDEPLOY. (The value is baked in at build time, so saving alone
#   does not update a live site.)
#
#   `/api` is the complete correct value - it is NOT a placeholder. Vercel
#   serves the engine at /api on the same domain as your website, so there
#   is no separate engine URL to find or create.
#
#   -> Python works. Java does NOT (Vercel has no JDK), so the Java button
#      is hidden automatically.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * The `VITE_` prefix is required: Vite only exposes variables with it to
#   frontend code. Never put secrets in a VITE_ variable - they end up
#   readable in the shipped JavaScript.
#
# * Read at BUILD time, not runtime. Changing it requires a rebuild/redeploy.
#
# * This file is a template only. Vite does not read it. To use a real local
#   override, copy it to `.env` (which is git-ignored). You do not need one.
# ============================================================================

# Local default (uncomment by copying this file to `.env` if desired):
VITE_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
